1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,165
A lending support team gets a constant

2
00:00:02,174 --> 00:00:03,633
stream of customer requests,

3
00:00:04,128 --> 00:00:06,734
and right now a person reads every single one.

4
00:00:06,899 --> 00:00:08,991
That's slow, it's inconsistent,

5
00:00:09,505 --> 00:00:12,202
and it depends on the judgment of whoever opens it.

6
00:00:13,211 --> 00:00:16,569
Handoff reads each request, works out what it is,

7
00:00:16,752 --> 00:00:18,239
and runs the whole workflow.

8
00:00:19,046 --> 00:00:22,275
Anything it isn't sure about, it hands to a person.

9
00:00:22,917 --> 00:00:26,294
This is the desk, running on two hundred committed cases.

10
00:00:26,844 --> 00:00:28,569
A billing dispute drafts a reply,

11
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:32,422
suppresses collections, sends it to the disputes team,

12
00:00:32,789 --> 00:00:35,101
and sets a follow-up against the SLA.

13
00:00:35,908 --> 00:00:39,303
A general enquiry is the only type the system can

14
00:00:39,312 --> 00:00:41,872
close on its own — and only when the answer is

15
00:00:41,881 --> 00:00:44,716
grounded in a knowledge base entry it can cite.

16
00:00:45,284 --> 00:00:48,954
A hardship case stops all automation as its first step,

17
00:00:49,211 --> 00:00:51,028
escalates, and never auto-resolves.

18
00:00:52,183 --> 00:00:53,963
Live mode runs the same pipeline

19
00:00:53,972 --> 00:00:55,376
on a message you paste in.

20
00:00:55,945 --> 00:00:58,275
This one is asking for a payoff statement.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,541
But read further down —

22
00:01:02,092 --> 00:01:04,642
the customer says they can't afford the payment,

23
00:01:05,101 --> 00:01:06,697
and threatens to go to the regulator.

24
00:01:07,266 --> 00:01:09,450
The model looks at the surface request,

25
00:01:09,459 --> 00:01:11,450
and calls it a service request.

26
00:01:12,128 --> 00:01:14,385
But two deterministic guardrails read

27
00:01:14,394 --> 00:01:17,284
what's underneath, and force it onto the

28
00:01:17,294 --> 00:01:19,431
hardship branch, at critical urgency.

29
00:01:20,257 --> 00:01:22,752
Guardrails can only escalate, never downgrade.

30
00:01:23,578 --> 00:01:26,110
A false alarm costs an agent two minutes.

31
00:01:27,229 --> 00:01:29,670
A missed hardship case is a compliance failure.

32
00:01:30,294 --> 00:01:33,248
Then the branch actually runs — automation paused,

33
00:01:33,688 --> 00:01:36,092
case escalated, supervisor alerted,

34
00:01:36,661 --> 00:01:39,229
and a reply drafted but held for a human to approve.

35
00:01:41,046 --> 00:01:42,954
Send the exact same message again,

36
00:01:43,303 --> 00:01:45,780
and it's caught as a duplicate by content fingerprint —

37
00:01:45,789 --> 00:01:47,982
before the model is even called.

38
00:01:48,495 --> 00:01:50,239
No double routing, and nothing spent.

39
00:01:50,917 --> 00:01:52,202
Now change the message,

40
00:01:52,459 --> 00:01:54,312
and switch every model provider off.

41
00:01:54,321 --> 00:01:57,156
The waterfall degrades through each tier,

42
00:01:57,358 --> 00:02:00,110
then falls back to the deterministic keyword floor.

43
00:02:00,679 --> 00:02:03,046
Its confidence is capped at zero point six,

44
00:02:03,156 --> 00:02:05,908
so it can never close a case on its own.

45
00:02:06,807 --> 00:02:09,486
When the system degrades it keeps working,

46
00:02:09,495 --> 00:02:11,431
but it never gets more independent.

47
00:02:12,349 --> 00:02:14,532
Any live case can be corrected,

48
00:02:14,862 --> 00:02:17,633
and the corrected branch runs again for real.

49
00:02:18,128 --> 00:02:19,927
The case keeps all three layers —

50
00:02:19,936 --> 00:02:22,367
what the model said, what the system decided,

51
00:02:22,624 --> 00:02:24,312
and what the human changed it to —

52
00:02:24,532 --> 00:02:26,440
stored as a labelled training pair.

53
00:02:27,523 --> 00:02:30,569
Corrections stack up without overwriting each other.

54
00:02:31,743 --> 00:02:34,752
And approving is a record that a person actually looked.

55
00:02:35,615 --> 00:02:39,211
That's three request types and three distinct branches,

56
00:02:39,706 --> 00:02:41,376
each executed end to end.

57
00:02:41,385 --> 00:02:44,202
Eighty-eight percent accuracy on a hundred

58
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:47,156
held-out cases, run once and scored once.

59
00:02:47,835 --> 00:02:50,532
The keyword floor on the same set gets forty-seven.

60
00:02:51,872 --> 00:02:52,771
Every branch finished.

61
00:02:54,092 --> 00:02:57,229
The model decides. The state machine executes.
